    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d721">

                <pb facs="0664" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/50</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-30T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>653. Your 1707 and 1688.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d721-f1"/> Department has advised
                    Finnish Commissioners here that it approves of initial shipment of 2,000 tons of
                    foodstuffs for Finland. British Government does not object.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
